of \\(B\\setminus U\\).  For the unique column\nwhose hole is in the top row (\\(r_j=1\\)) the upper tile is empty; for the\nunique column whose hole is in the bottom row (\\(r_j=n\\)) the lower tile is empty.\nHence the total number of tiles equals\n\\[\n2n-2.\n\\tag{4}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 8.  Conclusion\n\nThe construction in §7 shows that \\(2n-2\\) tiles are sufficient, while the\nargument in §§4–6 proves that no tiling can use fewer than \\(2n-2\\) tiles.\nTherefore the minimum possible number of tiles is exactly \\(2n-2\\).\n\nFor \\(n=2025\\) the minimum number is\n\\[\n2\\cdot2025-2=4048.\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{4048}\n\\]"
