8\\).\n\n---\n\n**### Detailed Solution**\n\nLet  \n\n\\[\nn=2025 .\n\\]\n\nMatilda must leave exactly one uncovered unit square in each row and each column.  \nDenote by  \n\n\\[\np:\\{1,\\dots ,n\\}\\longrightarrow\\{1,\\dots ,n\\}\n\\]\n\nthe permutation defined by the condition that the uncovered square in row \\(i\\) lies in column \\(p(i)\\).  \nThus the set of uncovered squares is  \n\n\\[\nU=\\{(i,p(i))\\mid i=1,\\dots ,n\\}.\n\\]\n\nAll other unit squares must be covered by pairwise disjoint axis‑aligned rectangular tiles.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 1.  An explicit tiling with \\(2n-2\\) tiles  \n\nPlace the uncovered squares on the main diagonal, i.e. choose \\(p(i)=i\\) for every \\(i\\).  \nIn row \\(i\\) the uncovered square splits the row into a left segment of length \\(i-1\\) and a right segment of length \\(n-i\\).\n\n* For each column \\(j\\;(1\\le j\\le n-1)\\) place a vertical tile covering the squares  \n\n  \\[\n  \\{(i,j)\\mid i=j+1,\\dots ,n\\},\n  \\]\n\n  which has size \\((n-j)\\times1\\).  \n  These \\(n-1\\) tiles cover all squares left of the diagonal.\n\n* For each row \\(i\\;(1\\le i\\le n-1)\\) place a horizontal tile covering the squares  \n\n  \\[\n  \\{(i,j)\\mid j=i+1,\\dots ,n\\},\n  \\]\n\n  which has size \\(1\\times(n-i)\\).  \n  These \\(n-1\\) tiles cover all squares right of the diagonal.\n\nThe two families are disjoint, each tile lies on grid lines, and every row and column contains exactly one uncovered square (the diagonal one).  \nHence a tiling with  \n\n\\[\n(n-1)+(n-1)=2n-2\n\\]\n\ntiles exists. Consequently\n\n\\[\n\\text{minimum number of tiles}\\le 2n-2. \\tag{1}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 2.  A lower bound of \\(2n-2\\) tiles  \n\nDefine the **left region**\n\n\\[\nL=\\{(i,j)\\mid 1\\le i\\le n,\\;1\\le j<p(i)\\},\n\\]\n\nand the **right region**\n\n\\[\nR=\\{(i,j)\\mid 1\\le i\\le n,\\;p(i)<j\\le n\\}.\n\